## SSA Spiller Crash Reproduction Rule

- Whenever a SSASpiller MIR test crashes, asserts, or segfaults while running under `llvm/test/CodeGen/AMDGPU/SSASpiller`, immediately reproduce it in `/work/atimofee/sandbox/bugs/ssa-spiller/tests/spiller`.
- Steps:
  1. `cp` the failing `.mir` from `llvm/test/CodeGen/AMDGPU/SSASpiller/` into `/work/atimofee/sandbox/bugs/ssa-spiller/tests/spiller/`.
  2. `cd /work/atimofee/sandbox/bugs/ssa-spiller/tests/spiller`.
  3. Run `/work/atimofee/sandbox/github/llvm-project/build/Debug/bin/llc` with the exact RUN line from the test (including all flags such as `--amdgpu-ssa-spill-markers=1`) and pipe into FileCheck if the RUN line does so.
- Always follow this protocol before debugging the failure further.

## SSA Spiller LIT Invocation Rule

- When running the SSASpiller LIT tests, always execute them directly from the test directory.
- Steps:
  1. `cd /work/atimofee/sandbox/github/llvm-project/llvm/test/CodeGen/AMDGPU/SSASpiller`
  2. Run `/work/atimofee/sandbox/github/llvm-project/build/Debug/bin/llvm-lit -v .` (note the trailing dot for “current directory”).
- Use this command instead of ninja shortcuts to ensure we exercise exactly the SSASpiller tests.
